  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leave No One Behind: Fostering Equality and Protection against Discrimination - Serbia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Leave No One Behind&quot; project aims to promote equality and protect vulnerable groups from discrimination in Serbia. It will introduce systematic changes to policy making processes by developing a methodology that ensures laws and policies consider diversity perspectives. By advocating for a more responsive strategic framework in the area of anti-discrimination and better implementation of planned measures, as well as improving accountability of national and local governments, the project seeks to enhance protection and support mechanisms for citizens facing discrimination. Additionally, by building the capacities of local organisations to provide community-based assistance regarding discrimination, the project will expand direct support to victims nationwide. Through these structural and functional improvements to legislation, strategic frameworks, and support networks, the project strives to create a more equitable and just society where the rights of every individual are protected and no one is left behind.</narrative>
  </description>
